WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.630
Remember Mission one: every step makes the snowflake's edge longer, and no step is ever the last.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.610
Keep going, and the edge becomes longer than any ruler.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:16.470
Now look: there's the snowflake, drawn on a single sheet of paper.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:23.130
An edge longer than any ruler, round a shape drawn on one page: surely both can't be true?

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.910
Can a shape with an infinite edge still fit on a page?

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:33.990
In this mission, you'll work out how much area the first step adds, as new triangles appear on each edge.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:39.110
You'll compare the second step with the first, and follow the area as the steps go on.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.470
Your mission: decide whether an infinite edge can fit on a page.
